    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d924">

                <pb facs="0821" n="809" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/25271: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kelley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-05T20:00:00+02:00">November 5, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 6—12:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1126. My 1115, November 4. British Ambassador<anchor n="9" xml:id="d924-f1"/>
                    made representations today to Foreign Minister regarding passage through Straits
                    of ships obtained by Germany from French Government and Minister took same
                    position as he did in his conversation with me.</p>
                <p>Soviet Chargé also called Minister today regarding matter and received a reply
                    similar to those received by British Ambassador and myself. Soviet Chargé has
                    been in some perplexity with regard <pb facs="0822" n="810" xml:id="pg810"/> to
                    execution of his rather rigid instructions which directed him either to call on
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs jointly with his British and American colleagues or
                    if visits were made separately to make his visit on same days those made by
                    Hugessen and myself. After being informed that both Hugessen and myself had
                    received instructions that I should make first approach he decided to make his
                    representations today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kelley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d924-f1" n="9" xml:id="d924-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Hughe M. Knatchbull-Hugessen.</p>
            </note>
